-- examples/checks/agg-join-delta-first-space.rofl — A PLAN THAT OUTGROWS THE SPACE IS NOT A WALL.
--
-- hit(A, C) :- a(A, B), b(B, C), c(C). The planner estimates b(B, k) at 18 rows a binding
-- (950 rows over 51 values of C) where 900 hold C = k: the plan from the news of c(k) holds
-- 900 rows, the written order a handful, and nothing is concluded. Two worlds read this file
-- under a space of 700 rows: one in written order, as every firing is under a wall a caller
-- set (agg_breaks `delta_first_walls`), one opted into the plans, where a plan that outgrows
-- the space is solved again in written order (agg_breaks `delta_first_overrun_holes`). Both
-- complete, as the TypeScript engine does.
-- expect-no-row: hole[$kernel]($rule(
-- expect-no-row: hit[main](
edb(a). edb(b). edb(seed).
c(C) :- seed(C).
hit(A, C) :- a(A, B), b(B, C), c(C).
